    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "JUNITEDBUSINESS\nmen u",
      "WELCOME\nEast and West blend\nbrilliantly on today's menu,\nwith an eclectic array of food\ncreated by United Airlines\nExecutive Chef Kanji Sato and\nhis team in Narita, working in\npartnership with United's\nCorporate Chef Eric Kopelow.\nNagano-born Chef Sato began\nhis culinary career at the\nPrince Hotels in Yokohama,\nMontreal and Toronto prior to\njoining United in Japan. He\ndesigned the expanded Obento\noffered on selected flights.\nChef Sato received the Five\nStar Diamond Award as one of\nthe World's Best Chets in\n1999 from The American\nAcademy of Hospitality\nSciences.\nChef Kopelow, a graduate of\nNew York's famed Culinary\nInstitute of America, has been\nawarded over 30 gold, silver\nand bronze medals from\nculinary competitions around\nthe world. Most recently, he\nwas inducted into both CIA's\nHall of Fame and the 2000-\n2001 Lexington's Who's Who\nRegistry of Executives and\nProfessionals.\nPlease enjoy these dishes on\ntoday's flight.\nd5ct\n***LiVe ViM=77=\n25LKt41P. 77\nThe American Academy of\nHospitality Sciences 2) #:#\nCA REnter = 70-12|\nC Five Star Diamond Award\nCulinary Institute of America\ntil Cit CIA's Hall of Fame \u0026\n2000-2001 Lexington's Who's\nWho Registry of Executives\nand Professionals DAy,-K\nAHHHHHH"
